    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk the keys seem fine and the card worked on a test site. i checked the payload and everything looks like its in the right format according to the docs. is there any way to see the specific reason for the 402 in the response body? like is stripe sending back a more detailed error message that i might be overlooking in the json?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, Stripe typically provides more detailed error information in the response body. To view the full error details, you can try using tools like cURL or Postman with the `--verbose` flag enabled, or intercepting the network request in the browser's developer tools using the 'Request' tab. This can be helpful for assessing the headers and body that were sent, and it may reveal additional error details that are passed under the hood within the JSON response. Just make sure to include your API key, and you should be able to troubleshoot the source of your 402 error. Misinterpretations of the data or security-related reasons such as CSP (Content Security Policy) can also lead to unexpected issues. You might want to double-check your server's CSP settings to ensure it's not preventing your request from reaching Stripe's server.",
